4. Vendored client halves — build/plugin-toggle.js, build/session-eva-status.js
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Both files started as byte-for-byte copies of code from other plugins, not written
for this theme (see the caveats at the end of this section). Both upstreams are MIT,
and both are by the same author as this theme:

  build/plugin-toggle.js
    Upstream: dsh-disable-unofficial-plugins
    Source:   https://github.com/WhatCannotBeSaid/dsh-disable-unofficial-plugins
    License:  MIT

  build/session-eva-status.js
    Upstream: dsh-session-eva-status v0.1.0
    Source:   https://github.com/WhatCannotBeSaid/dsh-session-eva-status
    License:  MIT

MIT requires its copyright notice and license text to travel with copies and
substantial portions. Both upstream repositories carry them in their own LICENSE
files; the full MIT text and the copyright line are section 1 of this
repository's LICENSE. Neither of these two files carries a notice of its own, and
both are inlined into the generated client.js, so if you redistribute either file
or the bundle, carry this section with it.

Two caveats, added 2026-10-09, the second amended 2026-10-10.
build/session-eva-status.js (D78) is no longer a byte-for-byte copy: this repository
patches three spots in its hot path — a frame-coalesced schedule, a
compare-then-write pin attribute, and cancelling the pending frame on dispose —
because the upstream checkout is not available here to fix and re-vendor.
build/plugin-toggle.js (D79) is patched in six spots. Five of them are
performance-only and none of those five is behavioural: a reload sequence guard, a
single-slot reload debounce, a compare-then-write button text, a throttled body
redraw, and a Set-based reason dedupe. The sixth (D82) does change behaviour, and is
the reason this file is no longer a faithful copy of upstream in any sense: upstream
excludes only the switch's own package from the batch, but this copy is vendored
into the theme's client bundle, so the theme itself is an unofficial plugin too and
would otherwise be offered up for disabling — by a button that the theme's own
bundle provides. The switch now excludes its host bundle as well. Both lists are at
the top of the respective file and pinned by the cli.27 and cli.28 checks in
tools/selfcheck.mjs; everything else in each file is still upstream's code.
Refreshing either file from upstream must re-apply them.


